 <br>\nSow in shallow drills in spring and keep <br>\nfree from weeds in summer. Mulch over winter <br>\nand the young blanched leaves will be ready for <br>\nuse early the following spring. <br>\nOz. <br>\nLarge Leaved \u2014 Pkt, 5c $ .40 <br>\nENDIVE. <br>\nSow the seed in June or July In shallow <br>\ndrills and thin the plants out to 6 inches apart. <br>\nWhen nearly full grown tie the outer leaves to- <br>\ngether to blanch. <br>\n1 oz. to 300 feet of drill. <br>\nLb. <br>\nGreen Curled \u2014 Leaves dark green and finely <br>\ncut, tender and hardy. Pkt., 5c; oz., <br>\n15c; y\u00b1 lb., 35c $1.00 <br>\nWhite Curled \u2014 Finely cut and very tender, <br>\neasily blanched. Pkt., 5c; oz., 15c;\u00a0% <br>\nlb., 35c 1.00 <br>\nGARLIC. <br>\nPlant in rows in rich soil. <br>\nGarlic Sets\u2014\u00a0% lb., 15c <br>\n.35 <br>\nKALE (Borecole). <br>\n1 oz. for 2000 plants. <br>\nExcellent fall and winter greens. Grow and culti- <br>\nvate the same as Cabbage. Sow the seed early, and <br>\ntransplant in rows 3 feet apart and 2 feet between the <br>\nplants in the row. <br>\nLb. <br>\nDwarf Green Curled Scotch\u2014 Leaves beautifully <br>\ncurled bright green, very tender. Pkt., 5c; <br>\noz., 10c;\u00a0% lb., 20c $ .65 <br>\nSiberian \u2014 Dwarf, large broad leaves, very hardy. <br>\nPkt., 5c; oz., 10c;\u00a0% lb., 20c 60 <br>\nDwarf Green Curled Scotch Kale. <br>\nJi, <br>\nGreen Curled Endive. <br>\n\u2022 HERBS. <br>\nFor winter use cut the varieties of which the stems and leaves <br>\nare used before the blossom appears, tie in bunches and hang in a <br>\ncool dry place. <br>\nLb. <br>\nBasil, Sweet \u2014 Used for flavoring soups and sauces. Pkt., 5c; <br>\noz., 15c; Vi lb., 50c $1.50 <br>\nBorage \u2014 For flavoring or bees. Pkt., 5c; oz., 15c;\u00a0% lb., 40c. 1.25 <br>\nCaraway \u2014 The seed is used for bread and confectionery. Pkt., <br>\n5c; oz., 10c; Vi lb., 25c . . . 75 <br>\nCoriander \u2014 Seeds used for confectionery. Pkt., 5c; oz., 10c; <br>\nM lb., 25c 75 <br>\nDill \u2014 Used in cucumber pickles. Pkt., 5c; oz., 10c;\u00a0% lb., 20c. .60 <br>\nFennel, Sweet \u2014 Used for soups, sauces and salad. Pkt., 5c; <br>\noz., 10c; Vi lb., 30c 1.00 <br>\nHorehound \u2014 Used for seasoning and medicinal purposes. Pkt., <br>\n5c; oz., 20c;\u00a0% lb., 60c 2.25 <br>\nLavender \u2014 Pkt., 5c; oz., 15c;\u00a0% lb., 35c 1.25 <br>\nMarjoram, Sweet \u2014 Used for seasoning. Pkt., 5c; oz., 20c; <br>\nYi lb., 50c 1.75 <br>\nMint \u2014 Plants, each, 15c; by mail, 25c. <br>\nSage \u2014 Used for seasoning and dressing. Pkt., 5c; oz., 15c; <br>\nM lb., 50c 1.50 <br>\nSummer Savory \u2014 Used for flavoring. Pkt., 5c; oz., 10c; y 4 lb., 25c. .75 <br>\nTarragon \u2014 Plants, each, 15c; by mail, 25c. <br>\nThyme, Broad Leaved \u2014 Used for seasoning. Pkt., 5c; oz., 25c; <br>\n% lb., 85c 3.00 <br>\n</p>\n13","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1912","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/biodivlibrary/16370928191\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/biodivlibrary/16370928191</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"A. Currie &amp; Company.; Henry G. Gilbert Nursery and Seed Trade Catalog Collection.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"37879809":{"pageid":37879809,"ns":6,"title":"File:Moretum, Ingredients (14964548651).jpg","index":2,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Moretum%2C_Ingredients_%28149